The implementation’s ordinary mathematical logic appears aligned with the contract: it peels decimal digits recursively and recurses over the list. I’m testing this with an independently generated corpus that covers the `-10/-9` and `9/10` helper boundaries, positive/nonpositive digit-sum branches, all boundary pairs, exhaustive singleton integers from −1000 through 1000, and 2,000 deterministic random lists. I’m also separating CPython recursion-resource behavior from value mismatches, since this is a partial-correctness audit.
